{
 "section_summary": "This section continues a guide to Japanese wartime production controls and recommends how Military Government could administer production after occupation. It covers national, regional and local control agencies, priorities, allocations, credit, personnel and reporting. Appendices list Japan’s 1945 administrative regions and reproduce the National Mobilisation Law, provisions of the Munitions Company Act and the opening of an account of the Munitions Superintendence Bureaus.",
