   "about": "Describes Japan’s wartime economic controls and recommends production policies for Military Government.",
   "summary": "The guide describes the powers and privileges of munitions companies, national policy companies and public corporations, then traces economic administration through regional and prefectural levels. It recommends occupation priorities for essential military and civilian goods, using allocations and credit to direct scarce supplies. It proposes retaining useful control machinery initially while abolishing wartime munitions and cartel bodies, supporting smaller producers, preserving records and gathering regular production reports. It also outlines central and regional Military Government production agencies.",
